\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. We praise| Thee, O| God: we
\par acknowledge| Thee to| be 
\par the| Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. All the| earth doth| worship
\par Thee: the| Father| ever-| lasting.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. To Thee all angels| cry a-| loud:
\par the heavens, and| all the| powers
\par there-| in.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. To Thee| cherubin, and| seraphin:
\par con-| tinual-| ly do| cry,
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Holy,| holy,| holy: Lord| God of|
\par Saba-| oth;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 6. Heaven and| earth are| full:
\par of the| majesty| of Thy| glory.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. The glorious company of the a-| postles|
\par praise Thee:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. The goodly fellowship| of the prophets|
\par praise Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9. The noble army of| martyrs| praise
\par Thee:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10. The holy Church throughout|
\par all the| world doth ac- | knowledge
\par Thee:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 11\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 11. The| Fa- | ther: of an| infinite
\par majes- | ty;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 12\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 12. Thine honourable, true and |
\par only| Son:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 13\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 13. Also the| Holy| Ghost the| 
\par Comforter.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 14\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par change
\par 14. Thou art the King of| Glory
\par O| Christ:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 15\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 15. Thou art the ever-| lasting|
\par Son of the| Father.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 16\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 16. When Thou tookest upon Thee
\par to de-| liver| man: Thou didst not
\par ab-| hor the| Virgin's| womb.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 17\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 17. When Thou hadst overcome the|
\par sharpness of| death: Thou didst open
\par the Kingdom of| Heaven to| all be- | lievers.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 18\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 18. Thou sittest at the right| hand of|
\par God: in the| glory| of the| Father.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 19\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 19. We believe that Thou shalt come
\par to| be our| Judge:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 20\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 20. We therefore pray Thee, help
\par Thy servants, whom Thou hast re- | deemed
\par with Thy| precious| blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 21\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 21. Make them to be numbered| with
\par Thy| saints: in| glory| ever-| lasting.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 22\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par change
\par 22. O Lord, save Thy people and| bless
\par Thine| heritage:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 23\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 23. Govern them and| lift them| up
\par for| ever.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 24\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 24. Day by day we| magnify| Thee:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 25\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 25. And we worship Thy | name ever|
\par would without| end.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 26\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 26. Vouchsafe, O Lord, to keep us
\par this| day without| sin:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 27\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 27. O Lord, have mercy up-| on us,
\par have| mercy up-| on us.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 28\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 28. O Lord, let Thy mercy lighten upon
\par us as our | trust is in | Thee:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 29\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 29. O Lord, in Thee have I trusted,
\par let me| never| be con- | founded.
